WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.270
April 1897.

2
00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.310
A monthly magazine arrives.

3
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:08.380
Inside: part one of a
serial about Martians.

4
00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:11.160
Its first chapter opens with astronomers:

5
00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.680
"Men like Schiaparelli
watched the red planet".

6
00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.220
A railway signal.

7
00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:17.490
A bookshelf.

8
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.910
Ordinary things for a reader in 1897.

9
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.800
Now the same novel sits on your phone.

10
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:28.700
What did a reader in 1897 see
in this story that we miss?

11
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.180
In this mission, you'll
meet the first readers,

12
00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.110
who read it month by month.

13
00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.960
You'll find out why
astronomers argued about lines,

14
00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:38.000
and canals, on Mars.

15
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:41.520
And you'll match quotations
to the two big contexts:

16
00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:43.600
Darwin, and empire.

17
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:48.920
Your mission: find out what a
reader in 1897 saw that we miss.
